      <memberdef kind="enum" id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914b" prot="public" static="no" strong="yes">
        <type></type>
        <name>verbosity</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::verbosity</qualifiedname>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914ba73be252ca82217b1458a25e6b4e99f15" prot="public">
          <name>silent</name>
          <initializer>= 0</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>No console output; only the exit code is returned. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914ba556966c7830465dc4623d62e32cec31d" prot="public">
          <name>quiet</name>
          <initializer>= 1</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Displays only the overall session summary; the TAP reporter also displays one result line per test suite, counted by the plan. The failed checks are not displayed. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914bafea087517c26fadd409bd4b9dc642555" prot="public">
          <name>normal</name>
          <initializer>= 2</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Displays test suite and test case results; the individual checks are shown only for failures. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914ba2c7aea4237e25b4f8ee3b0bf77d6fed0" prot="public">
          <name>verbose</name>
          <initializer>= 3</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Displays all results, including passed checks, for maximum detail. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The verbosity levels for test reporting. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914b" kindref="member">verbosity</ref></computeroutput> enumeration defines the available levels of detail for test output produced by the reporting system. These levels control the amount and type of information displayed during test execution, allowing users to tailor the output to their specific requirements.</para>
<para>The level is selected with the <computeroutput>--silent</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>--quiet</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>--verbose</computeroutput> command-line options, or with <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner__options_1aff30f0303a958a549a2f4b6e67db00d5" kindref="member">runner_options::verbosity_level</ref></computeroutput>; the default is <computeroutput>normal</computeroutput>. The console output is intended for the people who watch the tests run, while the optional output file is intended for the integration with other tools. With the TAP reporter, the level affects only the console output, and the output file always receives the full report. The human reporter is intended for the console; its output file receives the full report only with the <computeroutput>normal</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>verbose</computeroutput> levels, and is incomplete otherwise.</para>
<para>The <computeroutput>quiet</computeroutput> level tells whether the run failed, but not what failed: the failed checks, their locations, and their test cases are not displayed (except for a test case that aborts the test execution, when exceptions are not enabled, since the summary is never reached). To learn what failed, use the <computeroutput>normal</computeroutput> level, which displays in full only the failed test cases, or keep <computeroutput>quiet</computeroutput> and use the TAP reporter with an output file, which receives them. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
