      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>C++ header file with declarations for the µTest++ runner options. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header provides the <computeroutput>runner_options</computeroutput> structure, which holds the configuration of a test session (the reporter, the verbosity, the output file, the use of colours, the filter, and the listing of the test cases), together with the <computeroutput>reporter_kind</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>verbosity</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>colour_mode</computeroutput> enumerations used by its members.</para>
<para>The options are usually parsed from the command line by <computeroutput>runner::initialise (argc, argv)</computeroutput>; the applications without a command line, such as the embedded ones without semihosting arguments, can set them directly and pass them to <computeroutput>runner::initialise (options)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>All definitions reside within the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref></computeroutput> namespace, ensuring clear separation from user code and minimising the risk of naming conflicts.</para>
<para>The header is included through <computeroutput><ref refid="micro-test-plus_8h" kindref="compound">micro-test-plus.h</ref></computeroutput> and should not be included directly by user code. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
